# The tests carry a real bare git repository as a fixture (test/Aspire.Hosting.ServiceSources.Tests/
# Fixtures/sample-service.git). Its plumbing files (packed-refs, HEAD, config, ...) must reach the
# checkout byte-for-byte: without this, a developer whose git is configured to convert line endings
# (core.autocrlf=true, common on Windows) gets '\r\n' rewritten into files git itself parses one line
# at a time, corrupting every ref name and breaking any test that shells out to real git against it.
**/*.git/** -text
